<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>The U.S. government recently released a report calling on the technical community to proactively reduce the attack surface area of software infrastructure. The report emphasized memory safety vulnerabilities, which affect how memory can be accessed, written, allocated, or deallocated.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>The report cites this class of vulnerability as a common theme in the some of the most infamous cyber events, such as the Morris worm of 1988, the Heartbleed vulnerability in 2014, and the Blastpass exploit of 2023.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em><a href="https://twitter.com/herbsutter">Herb Sutter</a> works at <a href="https://twitter.com/Microsoft">Microsoft</a> and chairs the ISO C++ standards committee. He joins the show to talk about C++ safety.</em></p>


